# Button spacing

Pinned actions sit between the top bar and the bottom navigation. They keep a gap from both, and they do not shrink when the content between them grows.

- Bottom actions use `Footer`. On a tab screen pass `aboveTabs` so the control clears the floating tab bar. Elsewhere `Footer` clears the bottom safe area. The screen uses `skipBottomInset` so that inset is not applied twice.
- Scrollable content on a tab screen may run under the bar. Its content container still uses `useBottomControlInset(true)` so the last control can scroll fully into view.
- Header controls stay inside `ScreenHeader` or `HeaderWithBtn`. The row and the control use `Layout.MinControl` and `flex-shrink: 0`, so they stay below the status bar and do not collapse into the title.
- Take the tab-bar height, the gap, and the minimum control size from `Layout` in `design/styles.ts`. Do not add a one-off bottom margin on a single screen.

```tsx
const bottomInset = useBottomControlInset(true)

<WrapperScreen skipBottomInset>
  <ScreenHeader title='Tables' right={<SIconButton />} />
  <SList contentContainerStyle={{ paddingBottom: bottomInset }} />
  <Footer aboveTabs>
    <Button title='Log completed table' onPress={log} />
  </Footer>
</WrapperScreen>
```
